1
00:00:01,091 --> 00:00:03,093
[opening theme song playing]

2
00:00:04,177 --> 00:00:07,431
BLUE BOX

3
00:01:23,590 --> 00:01:29,930
BLUE BOX

4
00:01:30,680 --> 00:01:31,640
[thudding]

5
00:01:31,723 --> 00:01:33,475
EPISODE 10
IT'S NOT A GOOD THING

6
00:01:42,192 --> 00:01:43,193
[gasps]

7
00:01:49,533 --> 00:01:51,827
- It's starting to come off.
- [winces]

8
00:01:54,037 --> 00:01:55,747
Just stay in bed and sleep.

9
00:01:59,209 --> 00:02:00,585
[door closes]

10
00:02:00,669 --> 00:02:01,878
[door opens]

11
00:02:01,962 --> 00:02:03,004
[groans]

12
00:02:03,797 --> 00:02:04,965
[exclaims]

13
00:02:05,590 --> 00:02:08,677
<i>How could I possibly sleep after that?!</i>

14
00:02:10,428 --> 00:02:11,972
[birds chirping]

15
00:02:12,848 --> 00:02:13,890
[thermometer beeps]

16
00:02:14,558 --> 00:02:16,893
Thirty-six-point-five degrees.

17
00:02:16,977 --> 00:02:18,353
You're back to full health.

18
00:02:18,436 --> 00:02:19,855
Yeah, guess so.

19
00:02:20,689 --> 00:02:23,483
Then again,
you are looking a bit exhausted.

20
00:02:23,567 --> 00:02:24,901
Are you going to practice?

21
00:02:25,569 --> 00:02:26,611
I gotta.

22
00:02:27,195 --> 00:02:29,531
You can take the day off
for once, you know.

23
00:02:29,614 --> 00:02:32,409
You work so hard, both you and Chinatsu.

24
00:02:33,869 --> 00:02:34,911
Yeah, we do.

25
00:02:37,164 --> 00:02:39,916
[Taiki] <i>How am I not supposed
to be hung up on this?</i>

26
00:02:42,168 --> 00:02:44,588
<i>I need to focus on badminton right now.</i>

27
00:02:46,798 --> 00:02:48,174
<i>Her weight on me.</i>

28
00:02:49,759 --> 00:02:53,138
<i>The smell of her shampoo... the warmth of...</i>

29
00:02:54,598 --> 00:02:57,267
[screams, cries]

30
00:02:57,350 --> 00:02:59,686
That was way out of bounds.

31
00:02:59,769 --> 00:03:02,230
Taiki! Hey, bro!

32
00:03:02,314 --> 00:03:04,399
- You have a stomachache?
- [Taiki exclaims]

33
00:03:04,482 --> 00:03:06,484
If it's got you out here
yodeling like a freak,

34
00:03:06,568 --> 00:03:08,194
then you should just go home.

35
00:03:08,278 --> 00:03:09,696
Nope, I'm all good.

36
00:03:10,530 --> 00:03:12,407
What are you all up to, anyway?

37
00:03:13,158 --> 00:03:14,492
[Haryu] Cleaning the pool.

38
00:03:15,869 --> 00:03:17,412
Our homeroom teacher asked.

39
00:03:18,246 --> 00:03:21,374
The volleyball club is using the gym
for their practice match,

40
00:03:21,458 --> 00:03:23,460
so I'm killing time till it's over.

41
00:03:24,169 --> 00:03:27,297
I'm just doing it 'cause they said
they'd give me extra credit!

42
00:03:27,380 --> 00:03:29,716
[Haryu] Well, you're here.
Why don't you help us out?

43
00:03:29,799 --> 00:03:33,178
Oh, but I was planning on doing
some strength training and-- [gasps]

44
00:03:33,261 --> 00:03:34,554
[sparkling sound]

45
00:03:43,688 --> 00:03:45,023
[gasps softly]

46
00:03:47,275 --> 00:03:48,485
Count me in.

47
00:03:51,029 --> 00:03:53,448
- Careful not to get your socks wet.
- Got it.

48
00:03:54,032 --> 00:03:58,787
<i>It's not like I'm secretly hoping
to stay close to Chinatsu or anything.</i>

49
00:03:58,870 --> 00:04:01,456
<i>I just want to help them clean the pool.</i>

50
00:04:04,960 --> 00:04:06,461
[groans]

51
00:04:10,507 --> 00:04:13,468
[boy] Haryu, I heard you made
the cut for nationals.

52
00:04:14,386 --> 00:04:17,013
What are you doing
wasting your time cleaning a pool?

53
00:04:17,097 --> 00:04:18,431
[Haryu] I don't mind.

54
00:04:18,515 --> 00:04:21,768
They said I can use the pool
if I help them clean it, so.

55
00:04:21,851 --> 00:04:24,521
[laughs] A-ha!

56
00:04:24,604 --> 00:04:27,357
Haryu just wants to work
on his 25-meter sprint!

57
00:04:27,440 --> 00:04:28,775
This guy is off his nut.

58
00:04:28,858 --> 00:04:30,485
He's like a nuclear reactor.

59
00:04:30,568 --> 00:04:32,821
And you two are gonna
come hang out with me.

60
00:04:32,904 --> 00:04:34,030
[both] Huh?

61
00:04:34,114 --> 00:04:36,908
Swimming is great.
It's a full-body workout.

62
00:04:36,992 --> 00:04:38,159
No, I'm out!

63
00:04:38,243 --> 00:04:39,286
Wait! You...

64
00:04:39,369 --> 00:04:40,620
Taiki.

65
00:04:41,705 --> 00:04:42,998
Let me just say...

66
00:04:43,081 --> 00:04:45,375
You have more weaknesses
than just your smash.

67
00:04:45,458 --> 00:04:46,501
What?

68
00:04:47,460 --> 00:04:48,878
INCREASE MY SMASH PRECISION
- INOMATA

69
00:04:48,962 --> 00:04:52,382
- Why does everyone know my goal sheet?
- [Haryu] I mean, it's on the wall.

70
00:04:52,966 --> 00:04:56,261
In the qualifiers,
your match against Yusa,

71
00:04:56,970 --> 00:04:58,763
you started off pretty terrible,

72
00:04:59,347 --> 00:05:01,599
and you could
barely get your feet to move.

73
00:05:03,601 --> 00:05:07,188
<i>He's a first-year, and his skills
will be even better next year.</i>

74
00:05:08,898 --> 00:05:10,025
Don't get down.

75
00:05:10,108 --> 00:05:11,484
It's a waste of time, okay?

76
00:05:15,864 --> 00:05:18,116
[Taiki] You're right. I'm sorry.

77
00:05:18,950 --> 00:05:20,327
I mean, I don't care.

78
00:05:20,952 --> 00:05:23,955
Whether you lose or not in singles
doesn't matter to me.

79
00:05:24,039 --> 00:05:26,041
- [Taiki grunts]
- But then,

80
00:05:26,124 --> 00:05:28,585
if you're too bummed to play well at all...

81
00:05:28,668 --> 00:05:30,795
Huh? Isn't that right, Chii?

82
00:05:30,879 --> 00:05:33,006
Uh... What are you talking about?

83
00:05:33,840 --> 00:05:36,051
We were just saying
how nice the weather is.

84
00:05:36,134 --> 00:05:38,344
Mm. You're totally right. It is.

85
00:05:38,845 --> 00:05:40,013
Yep, sure is.

86
00:05:40,096 --> 00:05:41,556
That was all. Sorry.

87
00:05:42,140 --> 00:05:43,600
[Chinatsu] Mm-hm.

88
00:05:43,683 --> 00:05:44,809
[Taiki sighs]

89
00:05:45,518 --> 00:05:46,561
[Haryu] Hm.

90
00:05:47,687 --> 00:05:51,191
So, um, you made
any progress on that, or what?

91
00:05:51,274 --> 00:05:53,735
[exclaims, trembles]

92
00:05:53,818 --> 00:05:55,403
[Haryu] What is this reaction?

93
00:05:56,946 --> 00:05:59,449
If you don't wanna talk about it,
then we won't.

94
00:06:01,159 --> 00:06:04,537
Hm? Hm. Well...

95
00:06:04,621 --> 00:06:05,622
[Haryu] Hm?

96
00:06:05,705 --> 00:06:08,458
How do I know
if I even have a chance with her?

97
00:06:08,541 --> 00:06:09,542
HE HAS NO CLUE WITH GIRLS

98
00:06:09,626 --> 00:06:12,087
- Yikes.
- Yeah, I know! I have no game whatsoever!

99
00:06:12,170 --> 00:06:16,716
But I was just wondering if there happen
to be any general standards in this area.

100
00:06:17,300 --> 00:06:19,719
[Haryu] <i>This dude is going after Chii?</i>

101
00:06:19,803 --> 00:06:22,263
[Taiki] Like,
if she calls me by a nickname,

102
00:06:22,347 --> 00:06:25,058
or if we're alone together
in the same room.

103
00:06:25,141 --> 00:06:26,726
[Haryu] Depends on the person, man.

104
00:06:26,810 --> 00:06:29,020
Yep, yep, yep. That's what I thought.

105
00:06:29,104 --> 00:06:32,107
I figured there wasn't going to be
a simple answer. I knew that,

106
00:06:32,190 --> 00:06:34,651
- but still...
- Uh... What are you mumbling about?

107
00:06:34,734 --> 00:06:37,445
Yeah, but then again,
we are talking about Chii.

108
00:06:37,529 --> 00:06:38,738
[Taiki] Hm?

109
00:06:39,572 --> 00:06:41,908
[Haryu] She's not weird
around guys at all.

110
00:06:41,991 --> 00:06:44,744
She gets along equally
with guys and girls, you know.

111
00:06:44,828 --> 00:06:46,246
So true.

112
00:06:46,329 --> 00:06:47,747
That being said,

113
00:06:47,831 --> 00:06:51,292
I don't think she'd make physical contact
with someone she's not into.

114
00:06:52,085 --> 00:06:54,838
I think that's an area
where she keeps some separation.

115
00:06:54,921 --> 00:06:55,755
[Taiki gasps softly]

116
00:06:58,716 --> 00:07:00,844
[Taiki] <i>Okay, okay. Relax.</i>

117
00:07:01,469 --> 00:07:05,265
<i>My cooling patch was just coming loose.
There's no deeper meaning behind it.</i>

118
00:07:06,141 --> 00:07:08,393
<i>No point in randomly assuming things.</i>

119
00:07:14,816 --> 00:07:16,317
<i>Don't get your hopes up.</i>

120
00:07:17,610 --> 00:07:19,571
[water splashing]

121
00:07:22,532 --> 00:07:24,075
Cannonball!

122
00:07:26,244 --> 00:07:27,454
Don't jump in, idiot!

123
00:07:28,329 --> 00:07:30,582
It feels great! Get in, Taiki!

124
00:07:30,665 --> 00:07:32,208
I'll pass on this one,

125
00:07:32,292 --> 00:07:34,294
since I just recovered from a cold.

126
00:07:35,128 --> 00:07:37,380
All right, then, Nishida. Let's do this.

127
00:07:37,464 --> 00:07:39,007
Wait, what? What do you mean?

128
00:07:39,549 --> 00:07:41,176
[footsteps approaching]

129
00:07:42,552 --> 00:07:44,971
STORAGE ROOM

130
00:07:45,972 --> 00:07:47,724
Hi, Taiki. Good work out there.

131
00:07:48,850 --> 00:07:50,268
You too, good work.

132
00:07:51,519 --> 00:07:53,646
[Chinatsu] Did they make you
clean everything up?

133
00:07:53,730 --> 00:07:54,731
[Taiki] Yep.

134
00:07:54,814 --> 00:07:59,235
<i>Don't overthink it, Taiki!
Act like a normal human being. Chill out.</i>

135
00:07:59,319 --> 00:08:02,238
[chuckles]
Those no-good upperclassmen, huh?

136
00:08:02,864 --> 00:08:03,990
[gasps softly]

137
00:08:05,867 --> 00:08:07,035
[Taiki] <i>But you know what?</i>

138
00:08:07,118 --> 00:08:10,413
<i>Chinatsu doesn't seem like
she's concerned about it.</i>

139
00:08:11,331 --> 00:08:14,250
<i>Even though we're alone together.</i>

140
00:08:16,628 --> 00:08:17,629
I'll see you.

141
00:08:17,712 --> 00:08:19,881
Oh, but... Um... Wait, Chinatsu!

142
00:08:20,798 --> 00:08:22,759
I want to thank you for yesterday.

143
00:08:22,842 --> 00:08:24,177
Yesterday...

144
00:08:24,260 --> 00:08:26,054
Yeah, my fever's gone now.

145
00:08:26,137 --> 00:08:28,431
Uh. Oh, right. Yesterday.

146
00:08:29,849 --> 00:08:31,267
Yeah, you're welcome.

147
00:08:34,270 --> 00:08:35,271
All right.

148
00:08:37,315 --> 00:08:38,274
Huh?

149
00:08:41,444 --> 00:08:42,487
Uh, Taiki?

150
00:08:46,366 --> 00:08:48,493
[gasps, grunts]

151
00:08:48,576 --> 00:08:50,787
I'm sorry! I was just wondering... uh...

152
00:08:50,870 --> 00:08:52,247
Whe...

153
00:08:52,330 --> 00:08:55,083
Do you know where
I'm supposed to put this here bucket?

154
00:08:55,166 --> 00:08:57,085
- I think up there.
- [gasps]

155
00:08:57,168 --> 00:08:59,295
Oh, right you are! I didn't realize!

156
00:08:59,379 --> 00:09:00,338
Thanks so much.

157
00:09:01,130 --> 00:09:02,423
[chuckles]

158
00:09:02,507 --> 00:09:04,133
I'm gonna head out.

159
00:09:04,217 --> 00:09:05,260
Yeah.

160
00:09:06,970 --> 00:09:08,054
[sighs]

161
00:09:09,389 --> 00:09:10,682
<i>What am I doing?</i>

162
00:09:12,976 --> 00:09:16,729
<i>I need to be more careful. I know that.</i>

163
00:09:25,363 --> 00:09:26,823
Chinatsu, good work.

164
00:09:27,782 --> 00:09:31,536
Thank for your help earlier, even though
it was my job for the PE committee.

165
00:09:31,619 --> 00:09:33,830
- No, no problem. I had fun.
- Huh?

166
00:09:34,998 --> 00:09:37,834
Well, if it isn't
the Yamaguchi-Sato couple!

167
00:09:37,917 --> 00:09:39,586
[Yamaguchi] Come on, don't tease us.

168
00:09:39,669 --> 00:09:43,423
[laughs] Don't be so shy.
Seeing you two so in love is a good thing!

169
00:09:43,506 --> 00:09:44,841
[Yamaguchi] Jeez.

170
00:09:44,924 --> 00:09:47,010
[Nagisa] Yamaguchi has gotten
prettier and prettier

171
00:09:47,093 --> 00:09:48,886
ever since they started dating.

172
00:09:49,554 --> 00:09:51,848
Man, best years of our lives!

173
00:09:51,931 --> 00:09:53,516
[feel-good music playing]

174
00:09:55,435 --> 00:09:56,936
Once you decide you want one,

175
00:09:57,020 --> 00:09:59,480
you'll get a boyfriend in no time,
don't ya think?

176
00:09:59,564 --> 00:10:03,860
Mm. You saying that just made me realize
that I don't really want one.

177
00:10:04,902 --> 00:10:07,989
Basketball is what's up.
Aren't you the same?

178
00:10:08,781 --> 00:10:09,866
Yep. True.

179
00:10:12,952 --> 00:10:13,953
[girls chattering]

180
00:10:14,037 --> 00:10:15,872
[Chinatsu] What's going on
with volleyball?

181
00:10:15,955 --> 00:10:19,375
[Nagisa] Oh, I heard that girl
was transferring schools.

182
00:10:20,335 --> 00:10:22,128
Her grandma got sick or something.

183
00:10:22,211 --> 00:10:24,464
And, they didn't make it
to nationals, either.

184
00:10:26,090 --> 00:10:27,800
It's kinda selfish, but...

185
00:10:27,884 --> 00:10:30,386
I gotta say, I'm glad
you stayed on our team.

186
00:10:30,470 --> 00:10:33,014
Because of you, we are going to nationals.

187
00:10:33,097 --> 00:10:34,807
Well, it wasn't just me.

188
00:10:34,891 --> 00:10:37,393
We should be grateful
to the relative you're living with.

189
00:10:38,811 --> 00:10:40,897
- [chuckles softly]
- You know what, though?

190
00:10:40,980 --> 00:10:44,150
If there was a hot guy
also staying at your relative's house,

191
00:10:44,233 --> 00:10:47,070
by this point,
you might've had a budding romance.

192
00:10:47,153 --> 00:10:48,363
[coughing]

193
00:10:48,446 --> 00:10:50,323
I didn't say anything that crazy.

194
00:10:50,406 --> 00:10:53,201
It's weird to say
something like that out of the blue.

195
00:10:53,284 --> 00:10:55,370
Just think. Living in the same house,

196
00:10:55,453 --> 00:10:57,914
you'd see him all the time
even if you're too busy for dates.

197
00:10:58,539 --> 00:11:00,458
I feel like you'd never be
in a relationship

198
00:11:00,541 --> 00:11:02,251
unless there's someone that close.

199
00:11:02,835 --> 00:11:05,922
Living together with a guy,
you couldn't help but think about him.

200
00:11:07,632 --> 00:11:09,926
It's not as simple as you make it sound.

201
00:11:10,510 --> 00:11:12,512
Huh? You say something?

202
00:11:12,595 --> 00:11:14,931
Oh, no. It was nothing.

203
00:11:21,521 --> 00:11:23,940
- It's dinner time!
- Whoa! That looks good!

204
00:11:24,023 --> 00:11:27,193
- Wow, everything looks delicious!
- [Taiki] I'll take this one!

205
00:11:27,276 --> 00:11:30,196
- Hey there, sir. All good over here?
- You had better eat some vegetables!

206
00:11:30,279 --> 00:11:31,989
Ah! [gulps]

207
00:11:32,949 --> 00:11:33,825
Mighty good!

208
00:11:33,908 --> 00:11:35,410
Chinatsu, for you.

209
00:11:36,119 --> 00:11:37,620
Oh, thank you very much.

210
00:11:37,703 --> 00:11:40,832
It's really lovely
getting to grill out together.

211
00:11:41,374 --> 00:11:43,292
My wife is the queen of the barbecue.

212
00:11:43,376 --> 00:11:45,753
[Yukiko] Here.
You should have some, too, Chinatsu.

213
00:11:45,837 --> 00:11:46,838
Thank you, Yukiko!

214
00:11:46,921 --> 00:11:48,423
[happy music playing]

215
00:11:49,632 --> 00:11:50,758
[chuckles]

216
00:11:51,926 --> 00:11:53,845
Have as much as you'd like.

217
00:11:53,928 --> 00:11:55,388
[Chinatsu] It's really good.

218
00:11:55,471 --> 00:11:57,473
[Taiki] <i>She really does like eating.</i>

219
00:11:58,015 --> 00:11:59,851
Honey, more veggies please!

220
00:11:59,934 --> 00:12:01,185
Coming right up!

221
00:12:06,774 --> 00:12:07,733
I'll help.

222
00:12:07,817 --> 00:12:09,444
Oh, no. Don't worry about it.

223
00:12:09,986 --> 00:12:11,612
I got this covered, go eat.

224
00:12:12,447 --> 00:12:15,032
I want you to think of our house
as your own.

225
00:12:15,116 --> 00:12:18,619
Well, since I am at my own home,
I can't act like a guest, can I?

226
00:12:19,203 --> 00:12:21,664
Huh. That's very mature of you.

227
00:12:22,206 --> 00:12:23,374
I'm sorry.

228
00:12:23,458 --> 00:12:25,585
I guess I was the one being too formal.

229
00:12:26,461 --> 00:12:27,795
Oh. It's fine.

230
00:12:28,838 --> 00:12:31,466
I'm away from home
for my work so much, and...

231
00:12:31,549 --> 00:12:33,885
you and I haven't really gotten
to talk a lot.

232
00:12:34,469 --> 00:12:35,761
Anything bugging you?

233
00:12:36,345 --> 00:12:39,390
Like, my wife's weight loss gadgets
taking up the whole closet,

234
00:12:39,474 --> 00:12:42,477
or how all the sweets Grandpa recommends
are the weird ones.

235
00:12:43,102 --> 00:12:44,395
Not particularly.

236
00:12:44,479 --> 00:12:46,856
- [Taiki's dad] Oh, are you sure?
- [Taiki] Hm?

237
00:12:46,939 --> 00:12:50,401
[Chinatsu] I mean it.
You don't need to be so considerate of me.

238
00:12:50,485 --> 00:12:52,695
Well, I don't know if I agree with you.

239
00:12:53,362 --> 00:12:56,282
We're taking care
of someone else's daughter after all.

240
00:12:57,783 --> 00:13:01,412
It's our job to make sure that
you are comfortable while staying with us.

241
00:13:02,163 --> 00:13:03,414
[gasps softly]

242
00:13:03,498 --> 00:13:05,583
I just made myself sound cool,

243
00:13:05,666 --> 00:13:07,543
but I was hesitant at first,

244
00:13:07,627 --> 00:13:09,420
of having you as a guest here.

245
00:13:10,087 --> 00:13:10,922
But then,

246
00:13:11,881 --> 00:13:13,674
we were talking, and Yukiko said...

247
00:13:14,634 --> 00:13:17,178
[Yukiko] It's our responsibility,
so I'll step up too.

248
00:13:17,845 --> 00:13:20,973
Those two years are going
to be irreplaceable for Chinatsu!

249
00:13:21,057 --> 00:13:24,393
That time will be more important for her
than it will be for us.

250
00:13:24,477 --> 00:13:27,480
If there's a way that we can help her
during that period,

251
00:13:27,563 --> 00:13:30,191
then it's our duty as parents
to give her that.

252
00:13:31,275 --> 00:13:32,485
Those were her words.

253
00:13:33,277 --> 00:13:37,490
Anyway, Yukiko is the decision-maker
of the house, so I follow her lead.

254
00:13:37,573 --> 00:13:39,200
[Chinatsu] <i>He has his emotional moments.</i>

255
00:13:40,743 --> 00:13:43,204
[Taiki's dad] But I realized
that she had a point.

256
00:13:43,913 --> 00:13:47,833
I knew that you had this dream,
so I thought I needed to support you.

257
00:13:49,585 --> 00:13:54,632
But then, you went and actually made it
to nationals, and I'm very proud.

258
00:13:56,384 --> 00:13:58,386
I want to see you make it even further!

259
00:14:02,640 --> 00:14:04,725
- Yes.
- [Taiki] Dad,

260
00:14:05,685 --> 00:14:07,770
Mom needs yakisoba noodles.

261
00:14:07,853 --> 00:14:08,980
Roger that.

262
00:14:09,855 --> 00:14:12,233
[Taiki] <i>I wonder
what they were talking about.</i>

263
00:14:12,316 --> 00:14:14,485
- [Taiki's dad] They're not here.
- What?!

264
00:14:15,278 --> 00:14:16,487
What are we going to do?

265
00:14:16,571 --> 00:14:18,990
Grocery shopping was your job, right?

266
00:14:19,073 --> 00:14:20,783
[Taiki's dad] I thought
that I bought them.

267
00:14:20,867 --> 00:14:21,868
[Taiki] If Mom finds out,

268
00:14:21,951 --> 00:14:24,370
it's gonna be nothing
but brown rice for a month.

269
00:14:24,871 --> 00:14:26,497
[Chinatsu] I'll go pick some up.

270
00:14:27,164 --> 00:14:28,875
There's something I wanted anyway.

271
00:14:28,958 --> 00:14:30,209
What? Uh, okay.

272
00:14:30,835 --> 00:14:33,254
- I'll leave it up to you then.
- Sure thing.

273
00:14:33,880 --> 00:14:35,631
[Taiki] <i>They've gotten closer?</i>

274
00:14:35,715 --> 00:14:38,759
- Why don't you go with her Taiki.
- Huh?

275
00:14:39,385 --> 00:14:43,764
Look. We're not gonna have a young woman
walking on her own in the dark, son.

276
00:14:43,848 --> 00:14:45,516
Yeah, I totally get that, but...

277
00:14:46,767 --> 00:14:50,563
<i>But I don't know how much distance
I should keep from her on the way.</i>

278
00:14:53,065 --> 00:14:54,025
Then...

279
00:14:54,108 --> 00:14:56,152
I can just go on my own.

280
00:14:56,235 --> 00:14:58,571
[Taiki's dad]
That was not the point I was making.

281
00:14:59,071 --> 00:15:00,031
[Chinatsu] Taiki.

282
00:15:00,114 --> 00:15:01,198
[gasps]

283
00:15:04,327 --> 00:15:05,328
Shall we?

284
00:15:06,120 --> 00:15:08,623
Wait, where did Taiki and Chinatsu go?

285
00:15:08,706 --> 00:15:10,458
The two of them went to the store.

286
00:15:10,541 --> 00:15:12,043
Oh, they didn't have to do that.

287
00:15:12,126 --> 00:15:15,713
It's nice that you and her
got to catch up, just the two of you.

288
00:15:15,796 --> 00:15:17,465
I'm blown away by how mature she is

289
00:15:17,548 --> 00:15:20,092
especially since she's just
one year older than Taiki.

290
00:15:20,176 --> 00:15:22,053
That girl certainly has her act together.

291
00:15:22,762 --> 00:15:24,430
Mm. You're right.

292
00:15:25,181 --> 00:15:27,016
She's almost too together.

293
00:15:29,226 --> 00:15:30,561
[pensive music playing]

294
00:15:30,645 --> 00:15:32,021
We didn't forget anything?

295
00:15:32,104 --> 00:15:33,105
SUPERMARKET MIRAHERU

296
00:15:33,189 --> 00:15:34,565
No, I think we got it.

297
00:15:34,649 --> 00:15:36,525
<i>I am halfway through!</i>

298
00:15:37,360 --> 00:15:38,569
Let's head home.

299
00:15:39,153 --> 00:15:42,490
[Taiki] <i>I managed to get by on chitchat
for the first half of this,</i>

300
00:15:43,157 --> 00:15:45,576
<i>but I've run out of things to talk about.</i>

301
00:15:45,660 --> 00:15:48,746
<i>Should I apologize again
for grabbing her arm?</i>

302
00:15:48,829 --> 00:15:49,914
<i>Hmm, but...</i>

303
00:15:49,997 --> 00:15:51,165
I guess...

304
00:15:52,458 --> 00:15:54,961
I shouldn't eat
a popsicle right now, right?

305
00:15:55,044 --> 00:15:56,212
Popsicle?

306
00:15:56,295 --> 00:15:59,131
I really want one,
but then I think of yakisoba...

307
00:15:59,215 --> 00:16:01,592
[Taiki] <i>That's what
you've been thinking about?</i>

308
00:16:01,676 --> 00:16:02,969
There's enough for everyone,

309
00:16:03,052 --> 00:16:05,596
so I should just wait,
and we can have them together.

310
00:16:06,263 --> 00:16:07,598
[laughs]

311
00:16:08,265 --> 00:16:12,186
[Taiki] <i>Chinatsu... Even she has
childish thoughts sometimes.</i>

312
00:16:13,813 --> 00:16:15,106
{\an8}Here.

313
00:16:16,649 --> 00:16:18,609
It's one of our family rules.

314
00:16:18,693 --> 00:16:21,112
When we have a barbecue,
you can eat whatever you want.

315
00:16:22,154 --> 00:16:23,406
[exclaims]

316
00:16:24,699 --> 00:16:26,117
That's a great rule!

317
00:16:28,828 --> 00:16:30,746
It's my mom's policy.

318
00:16:30,830 --> 00:16:32,123
I'll have one.

319
00:16:32,957 --> 00:16:35,126
Taiki, I think that you
take after your mother.

320
00:16:35,209 --> 00:16:36,043
Huh?

321
00:16:36,127 --> 00:16:38,921
You don't have to make
such a disgusted face, come on.

322
00:16:39,005 --> 00:16:43,217
Listen, I can't say that I'm ecstatic
to hear that I'm similar to my mother.

323
00:16:43,300 --> 00:16:44,343
You aren't?

324
00:16:44,427 --> 00:16:46,429
You're upbeat, energetic, and genuine.

325
00:16:46,512 --> 00:16:48,973
Altogether, you're a lot like her
if you ask me.

326
00:16:50,349 --> 00:16:54,645
Hm. Well, for you,
I feel like you take after your father.

327
00:16:56,397 --> 00:16:58,649
Your mom seemed more easygoing.

328
00:16:58,733 --> 00:17:00,860
Maybe. I'll have to think about it.

329
00:17:00,943 --> 00:17:04,655
Because with my dad, it's always hard
to tell what's going on in his head.

330
00:17:04,739 --> 00:17:06,699
[Taiki] <i>She does take after her dad.</i>

331
00:17:07,283 --> 00:17:10,661
When I mentioned to him that I wanted
to move into your family's house,

332
00:17:12,121 --> 00:17:15,416
<i>I thought he'd be against it,
but he ended up saying</i>

333
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:17,209
<i>"I see."</i>

334
00:17:17,293 --> 00:17:18,919
<i>That's all he had to say.</i>

335
00:17:19,003 --> 00:17:22,590
Like, I'm sure my mom
had told him about it in advance.

336
00:17:22,673 --> 00:17:24,925
But I was hoping for a bit more than that.

337
00:17:25,801 --> 00:17:27,470
I ended up taking it to mean,

338
00:17:27,553 --> 00:17:30,097
"That's your decision,
so follow through on it."

339
00:17:30,931 --> 00:17:33,017
[chuckles] He's not too good with words.

340
00:17:37,605 --> 00:17:39,065
[vehicle approaching]

341
00:17:39,148 --> 00:17:40,441
[grunts] Watch out!

342
00:17:46,072 --> 00:17:47,448
[Taiki gasps]

343
00:17:48,115 --> 00:17:49,241
[Chinatsu gasps]

344
00:17:52,286 --> 00:17:54,497
Sorry! Uh...

345
00:17:54,580 --> 00:17:57,208
<i>Dang it! I touched her again
without thinking.</i>

346
00:17:59,418 --> 00:18:02,296
Sorry, I should be walking
on the street side anyway.

347
00:18:02,379 --> 00:18:03,214
Taiki...

348
00:18:04,006 --> 00:18:06,217
So about what happened the other day.

349
00:18:06,801 --> 00:18:08,219
The other day?

350
00:18:09,178 --> 00:18:11,305
The day when you spiked a fever.

351
00:18:12,264 --> 00:18:13,849
Let's forget about it.

352
00:18:13,933 --> 00:18:15,976
- [gasps]
- [wind blowing]

353
00:18:18,521 --> 00:18:19,855
[sad music playing]

354
00:18:20,481 --> 00:18:21,607
Honestly, I...

355
00:18:22,191 --> 00:18:24,860
was acting carelessly considering I'm...

356
00:18:25,444 --> 00:18:26,862
living with a guy.

357
00:18:27,613 --> 00:18:31,867
It wasn't a good thing to do,
as someone who's in your family's care.

358
00:18:36,455 --> 00:18:39,708
So, I won't do anything like that again,

359
00:18:39,792 --> 00:18:40,876
going forward.

360
00:18:43,504 --> 00:18:44,463
Let's go.

361
00:18:55,057 --> 00:18:56,142
[Taiki] <i>What?</i>

362
00:18:57,309 --> 00:19:00,563
<i>She just... set a boundary between us.</i>

363
00:19:02,231 --> 00:19:03,440
[door opens]

364
00:19:03,524 --> 00:19:04,692
[Chinatsu] We're back.

365
00:19:05,734 --> 00:19:09,155
[Taiki] <i>And I got the sense that
she's aware of how I feel about her.</i>

366
00:19:10,698 --> 00:19:11,740
<i>She's good.</i>

367
00:19:13,701 --> 00:19:16,745
<i>She was encouraging me to have high hopes.</i>

368
00:19:16,829 --> 00:19:19,498
<i>And then she goes
and draws a line between us.</i>

369
00:19:21,625 --> 00:19:22,668
[music fades]

370
00:19:25,254 --> 00:19:27,673
Okay, everybody,
summer break starts tomorrow...

371
00:19:27,756 --> 00:19:28,632
SUMMER BREAK

372
00:19:28,716 --> 00:19:30,676
...but keep yourselves in check, all right?

373
00:19:31,260 --> 00:19:34,180
Try and aim to do things in moderation,
and make sure--

374
00:19:34,263 --> 00:19:35,764
- [bell chimes]
- [boy 1] Sir, yes, sir!

375
00:19:35,848 --> 00:19:38,392
- [boy 2] Buh-bye, teach!
- [teacher] Now hold on a minute!

376
00:19:38,475 --> 00:19:39,935
[students chattering]

377
00:19:41,270 --> 00:19:44,815
It's summer break, and yet your energy
is really bringing me down.

378
00:19:44,899 --> 00:19:47,568
I get it. You're pissed
about the homework?

379
00:19:47,651 --> 00:19:49,195
- Feel that.
- That's not it.

380
00:19:49,278 --> 00:19:52,489
[Hina] You tryna tell me you're not
against having homework on our break?

381
00:19:52,573 --> 00:19:54,241
No, that's not it either.

382
00:19:54,325 --> 00:19:55,367
[Hina] Thought so.

383
00:19:56,118 --> 00:19:57,453
Ooh, lightbulb moment!

384
00:19:58,245 --> 00:19:59,914
We hole up in the library,

385
00:19:59,997 --> 00:20:02,583
and do it together
after practice Saturday!

386
00:20:02,666 --> 00:20:04,460
[chuckles] Good, right?

387
00:20:04,543 --> 00:20:07,379
And I'm betting
that you wanna copy our answers.

388
00:20:07,463 --> 00:20:09,006
- [Hina whistles]
- [Ito] Um...

389
00:20:09,089 --> 00:20:09,965
[all] Hm?

390
00:20:10,591 --> 00:20:12,927
Would you mind
if we joined in on that too?

391
00:20:13,552 --> 00:20:15,596
- And me, also!
- Yeah, totally!

392
00:20:15,679 --> 00:20:16,931
We'll all go then!

393
00:20:17,014 --> 00:20:18,724
[Ito] Thanks, you're the best.

394
00:20:18,807 --> 00:20:21,477
<i>- Hey, could you help me with my Spanish?</i>
- [Hina] <i>I am loving this!</i>

395
00:20:23,938 --> 00:20:26,482
[Hina] Now we don't have to worry
about homework anymore.

396
00:20:26,565 --> 00:20:28,400
We haven't started yet.

397
00:20:28,484 --> 00:20:29,860
I am so excited!

398
00:20:29,944 --> 00:20:33,030
There are a ton of things
I wanna do over summer break!

399
00:20:33,113 --> 00:20:35,449
Won't you be prepping
for nationals, though?

400
00:20:35,532 --> 00:20:36,909
I mean, I will.

401
00:20:36,992 --> 00:20:39,787
But badminton has practice
almost every day, too, right?

402
00:20:39,870 --> 00:20:40,746
That's right.

403
00:20:41,330 --> 00:20:42,248
[Hina sighs]

404
00:20:45,084 --> 00:20:47,503
- Oh, Chinatsu.
- [Taiki exclaims]

405
00:20:49,588 --> 00:20:50,506
[Hina] She saw us!

406
00:20:55,261 --> 00:20:56,887
- [Kyo] Hm?
- [Hina] Huh?

407
00:20:58,097 --> 00:20:59,723
Why are you hiding down there?

408
00:20:59,807 --> 00:21:00,766
[Taiki groans]

409
00:21:01,433 --> 00:21:04,687
I'm not hiding.
There was a pencil lead on the floor.

410
00:21:04,770 --> 00:21:06,146
You really suck at lying.

411
00:21:07,690 --> 00:21:09,275
[Taiki] It really is nothing.

412
00:21:10,484 --> 00:21:13,070
My family had a barbecue the other day,

413
00:21:13,153 --> 00:21:14,738
and everyone's getting along.

414
00:21:15,406 --> 00:21:16,532
It's just...

415
00:21:17,449 --> 00:21:19,410
We got close to each other, physically,

416
00:21:19,493 --> 00:21:21,787
and, apparently,
she thinks it's not a good thing.

417
00:21:22,579 --> 00:21:24,331
She said that to me and...

418
00:21:24,415 --> 00:21:27,293
I'm just a little confused
on what I'm supposed to do.

419
00:21:29,586 --> 00:21:31,213
[sad piano music playing]

420
00:21:33,507 --> 00:21:35,426
All right. To practice!

421
00:21:59,658 --> 00:22:01,660
SUMMER BREAK

422
00:22:05,456 --> 00:22:07,458
[closing theme song playing]
